This notebook predicts forest above-ground biomass from multi-source satellite data: Sentinel-2 optical bands, Sentinel-1 C-band radar, and ALOS PALSAR L-band radar. It first cleans the data by removing invalid biomass values (such as the -9999 no-data placeholder) and rows with missing values. It then adds an NDVI feature from the red and near-infrared bands and splits the data by tile so the validation areas stay unseen during training. A linear regression with a Yeo-Johnson-transformed target serves as the baseline, compared against a LightGBM model with early stopping, both evaluated by RMSE. The final LightGBM model is retrained on all the clean data, fills missing test values with training-set medians, and generates predictions for all 45,019 test rows in the competition's submission format.
